ven coordinate, not code the image executes.\n\n**Root cause (verified by reproduction):** `org.hibernate:hibernate-spatial:8.0.0.Beta1` is a Maven *relocation POM* (packaging `pom`, `<distributionManagement><relocation>`) pointing to `org.hibernate.orm:hibernate-spatial:8.0.0.Beta1`. The real artifact's Gradle module metadata declares dual capabilities (`org.hibernate:hibernate-spatial` and `org.hibernate.orm:hibernate-spatial`) and imports `org.hibernate.orm:hibernate-platform` (a BOM) with `endorseStrictVersions: true`. The platform BOM in turn declares a dependency constraint back on `org.hibernate:hibernate-spatial:8.0.0.Beta1` itself. This self-referential constraint loop through the old-groupId relocation makes Gradle report `Component is the target of multiple version constraints with conflicting requirements` — a real upstream Hibernate 8 publishing quirk, reproduced locally with a minimal Gradle project.\n\nSwitching the test dependency to the new coordinate `org.hibernate.orm:hibernate-spatial:8.0.0.Beta1` resolves cleanly (verified: full dependency tree resolves, no conflict). The existing test's imports (`org.hibernate.spatial.integration.SpatialInitializer`, `org.hibernate.boot.registry.StandardServiceRegistryBuilder`) are present unchanged in the 8.0.0.Beta1 jars, and the test needs no database/Docker (it only builds a `StandardServiceRegistryBuilder`, no connection).\n\n```json\n{\n  \"action\": \"advisory_preparation\",\n  \"summary\": \"org.hibernate:hibernate-spatial:8.0.0.Beta1 is a Maven relocation POM to org.hibernate.orm:hibernate-spatial, and its platform BOM has a self-referential constraint back through the old groupId, causing Gradle to fail resolution with a version-constraint conflict; using the new org.hibernate.orm groupId for this version resolves cleanly.\",\n  \"deterministic_setup\": [],\n  \"agent_guidance\": \"For libraryVersion 8.0.0.Beta1 (and any other org.hibernate.orm-era 8.x version), change the generated build.gradle's testImplementation coordinate from \\\"org.hibernate:hibernate-spatial:$libraryVersion\\\" to \\\"org.hibernate.orm:hibernate-spatial:$libraryVersion\\\". The old org.hibernate:hibernate-spatial coordinate is only a relocation stub for 8.x and fails Gradle dependency resolution (\\\"Component is the target of multiple version constraints with conflicting requirements\\\") due to a self-referential constraint in org.hibernate.orm:hibernate-platform's BOM. Verified locally: the org.hibernate.orm coordinate resolves the full graph without conflict, and the existing test's imports (org.hibernate.spatial.integration.SpatialInitializer, org.hibernate.boot.registry.StandardServiceRegistryBuilder) are unchanged in the 8.0.0.Beta1 jars, so no other source changes are needed. No database or Docker image is required — the existing test only builds a StandardServiceRegistryBuilder.\",\n  \"risks\": [\n    \"If this repository's existing tests for org.hibernate:hibernate-spatial (6.5.0.Final, 7.2.0.Final) still use the old org.hibernate groupId, the fix must be conditional on version (e.g. only for 8.x+) rather than a blanket coordinate change, or applied per-version-directory.\",\n    \"8.0.0.Beta1 is a pre-release; upstream may still change the relocation/BOM structure before GA, so this workaround should be re-verified against later 8.x releases before generalizing.\"\n  ]\n}\n```","ttft_ms":6366,"type":"result","duration_ms":145290,"uuid":"48dbb400-8c8c-46f1-bbde-b515fa19115d","ttft_stream_ms":1204,"time_to_request_ms":85,"first_content_frame_ms":1204,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}

